
Flask ML Application Workflow
=============================

User
  ↓
Flask App
  ↓
main.py
  ↓
Load ML Model
  ↓
User Input
  ↓
ML Model Processing
  ↓
Prediction / Output
  ↓
HTML Template
  ↓
Result shown to User

=========

Project structure shown in your image
Flask-ML-App/
│
├── main.py
│
├── model.pkl
│
├── templates/
│   └── index.html
│
└── static/
    └── style.css

==========

What each file does

main.py → Main backend file. Controls the Flask application.

templates/index.html → Frontend page where the user enters input and sees the result.

static/style.css → Design and styling.

model.pkl → Your trained Machine Learning model.

=======

Complete flow
index.html
(User enters data)
        ↓
Flask / main.py
        ↓
Load model.pkl
        ↓
ML Model processes input
        ↓
Prediction Result
        ↓
main.py
        ↓
index.html
(Display output)
        ↓
User

========

So the main concept your trainer is teaching is:

Frontend (HTML) → Flask Backend (main.py) → ML Model (.pkl) → Prediction → Backend → Frontend

This is specifically a Flask Machine Learning web application workflow.

This Flask ML workflow is complete once the backend validates the submitted values before 
passing them to model.pkl for prediction and rendering the result in index.html, which prevents invalid input from reaching the model.

